-- title:
--   Constant-term section at ∞ on the j⁻¹-chart
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $K$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ over $L$, and let $A$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$ via the scalar tower. Let $j \in K$ be an element whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the rational power series $jNumQ$, and assume $j \neq 0$. Write $A_\infty$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgInf A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L137), the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$. The assertion is that there exists a ring homomorphism $\psi : A_\infty \to A$ such that: $\psi$ restricted along $A \to A_\infty$ is the identity on $A$; for every $f \in A_\infty$ and every integer $k < 0$, the $q^k$-coefficient of the image of $f$ in $L((q))$ vanishes; for every $f \in A_\infty$, the image of $\psi(f)$ in $L$ equals the $q^0$-coefficient of $f$; and $\psi$ sends the element $j^{-1}$ of $A_\infty$ to $0$.
--
--   This is the cusp $\infty$ realised as an $A$-valued point of the $j^{-1}$-chart of the two-chart integral model: elements of the chart ring have non-negative $q$-order, and taking the constant term of the $q$-expansion is a ring homomorphism to $A$ killing $j^{-1}$. It is used by the full-level results producing the constant-term homomorphism on the $j^{-1}$-chart of the integral model over a level field, in particular in levels two and three.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_ringHom_chartAlgInf_algebraMap_eq_coeff_zero_of_coe_eq_coeffEmb_jq.lean

